  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 1250 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nA weather system into the weekend still bears watch for the return \nof precipitation chance and cooler temperatures, though limiting \nfactors/evolution remain apparent. \n\nOverall, the trend over the last several runs of model guidance\nremains for a less-amplified/more sheared upper wave translating \nacross the north-central Great Plains on Saturday. The resultant \nweaker surface reflection, combined with a relatively dry/modified\nreturn-flow airmass, is leading to decreasing chances for \nrain/storms on Saturday, with only very low potential across \ncentral and eastern Oklahoma into the evening/nighttime hours. \n\nWhile not the strongest fall front, peak temperature readings may\nfall by 10+ degrees (compared to Saturday) in the post front on \nSunday. The best chance for rain/storms in the period may \nactually occur into/on Monday as a stronger southern stream upper\nsystem approaches from the southwest.\n\nUngar",
